Z||000008||Ferrari355||03-15-2000||01:28 PM||||Hey, I took some pics awhile back when this guy who worked at autozone said he had an 86 GT but it looked like a lambo kit and i was like whoa becasue i have looked up hundreds of kit car sites and and read tons of info on them and i took pics if anyone wants them. I'll scan them and post them. It's an IGF non stretch Countach 5000s kit car. I'll try to get the pics posted soon and Darklord, you can post them on your webpage if you want. Just e-mail me with the information you need and i'll see what i can do. Later  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||03-15-2000||04:07 PM||||my website is  <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> <P>to make it easier to send me photos, I'll make a directory on my server for uploading images. (via anonymous FTP) Inside that directory, just make a new directory with your name, or "lambopics" etc. and upload the photos there. Then just send off an email to   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   saying you've uploaded them.. I can't accept large file attachments anymore, my ISP (Primeline) deletes anything over 1mb now.. (and if a large attachment fills that up, any email messages I get after that are deleted.)<P>so if you must email, send them to the  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  address, not steve@primeline.net<P>thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-15-2000).]||||reg||1
